.TH GRAPHSYNCCTL 1 "November 2026" "plasma-graphsync-linux @PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
graphsyncctl \- command-line tool of Graph Sync, the OneDrive and SharePoint sync client for KDE Plasma
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B graphsyncctl
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B graphsyncctl
sets up accounts and sync locations, talks to the running sync service
.BR graphsyncd (1)
and works on single synced files.
Most users use the app
.BR plasma-graphsync-linux (1)
instead; this tool is for terminals, scripts and support.
.PP
A location syncs with its own account. The
.I current account
is the one new locations and the app use; files are always handled with the account of the
location they are in.
.SH ACCOUNTS
.TP
.B configure \-\-client\-id \fIID\fP \-\-tenant\-id \fITENANT\fP
Store the app registration for signing in: its client ID, and a tenant ID, domain or work e-mail
address.
.TP
.BR login " [" device ]
Sign in the current account (or the configured registration) in the browser, or with a code
entered at Microsoft's device login page.
.TP
.B logout
Sign out the current account; its locations stop syncing, the local files stay.
.TP
.B whoami
Show the current account and its OneDrive storage.
.TP
.B accounts
List the accounts on this computer and their locations; the current one is marked with *.
.TP
.BR add\-account " \fIEMAIL\fP [" device "] [\-\-client\-id \fIID\fP]"
Sign in another account, of another organisation or another user; it becomes the current
account. Without \-\-client\-id the suite's app registration is used.
.TP
.B use\-account \fIACCOUNT\fP
Make an account the current one.
.TP
.BR approval\-link " \fIEMAIL\fP|\fIDOMAIN\fP [\-\-client\-id \fIID\fP]"
Print the page where an administrator of that organisation approves the app registration once.
.SH LOCATIONS
.TP
.B add\-personal \fR[\fP\-\-local \fIPATH\fP\fR]\fP
Sync the current account's own OneDrive.
.TP
.B drives \-\-site\-url \fIURL\fP
List the document libraries of a SharePoint site.
.TP
.B add\-root \-\-name \fIN\fP \-\-local \fIPATH\fP \-\-drive \fIID\fP \fR[\fP\-\-remote\-root \fIITEM\fP\fR]\fP
Add a library (or one folder of it) as a location of the current account.
.TP
.B roots
List the locations.
.TP
.B remove\-root \fIROOT\fP
Stop syncing a location; the local files stay.
.TP
.B sync \fIROOT\fP \fR[\fP\-\-download\-only\fR]\fP
Run one sync cycle of a location in this process, with that location's account.
.SH RUNNING SERVICE
.TP
.BR status " | " activity
Show the state of the sync service and the recent activity (JSON).
.TP
.BR sync\-now " | " pause " [\fIMINUTES\fP] | " resume
Sync at once, pause (for some minutes, or until resumed) or resume.
.TP
.B migrate
Take over an install of plasma-onedrive-linux, the name before 0.7.0 (run once at login).
.SH FILES IN SYNCED FOLDERS
These use the account of the location the file is in, and fail when that account is no longer on
this computer.
.TP
.B item \fIPATH\fP
Show the online item (ids, web address, account).
.TP
.B link \fIPATH\fP \fR[\fPview|edit\fR] [\fPanonymous|organization|users\fR]\fP
Create a sharing link; without a scope the organisation's default link.
.TP
.BR permissions " \fIPATH\fP | " unshare " \fIPATH\fP \fIPERMISSION\fP"
List who has access, or remove a link.
.TP
.B invite \fIPATH\fP \fIEMAIL\fP \fR[\fPread|write\fR]\fP
Give someone access (no invitation e-mail is sent).
.TP
.B people \fITEXT\fP
Name suggestions from the current account's organisation.
.TP
.BR versions " \fIPATH\fP | " get\-version " \fIPATH\fP \fIVERSION\fP \fITARGET\fP | " restore\-version " \fIPATH\fP \fIVERSION\fP"
List the versions of a file, save one, or make one current again.
.TP
.B download \fIPATH\fP \fITARGET\fP
Save the current online content of a synced file.
.TP
.B add\-shortcut \fIFOLDER\fP
Add a synced folder to "My files" ("Add shortcut to My files").
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/graphsyncrc
Settings and locations.
.TP
.I ~/.config/graphaccountsrc
Accounts, shared with the other apps of the suite.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/graphsync/
Sync state per location.
.PP
Sign-ins are kept in KWallet (service "plasma-graphsync-linux").
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error (printed on standard error).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plasma\-graphsync\-linux (1),
.BR graphsyncd (1)
.PP
https://github.com/nvaert1986/plasma-graphsync-linux
